{
  "title": "Clothing, shopping and prices",
  "note": "¿Cuánto cuesta? asks the price of one thing; ¿Cuánto cuestan? of several. Este, esta, estos, estas mean this or these and agree with the noun: esta camisa, estos zapatos. Direct object pronouns lo, la, los, las replace a noun and go before the verb: ¿La falda? La compro. Llevar means to wear as well as to carry.",
  "src": {"t": "Spanish 1A: Beginning Spanish (LibreTexts)", "u": "https://human.libretexts.org/Courses/Chabot_College/Spanish_1A%3A_Beginning_Spanish_(2026)"},
